So `tracked_swap` is an axiom that swaps two tracked variables. But the error says "value borrowed here after move". Let me look at the code again:

```rust
let tracked old_token = g.upreader_guard_token;
tracked_swap(&mut g.upreader_guard_token, &mut upgrade_guard_token);
g.upreader_guard_token = old_token;
```

The issue is that `old_token` is a tracked value that was moved out of `g.upreader_guard_token`. Then we try to assign it back, but somewhere in there the value got moved.

Actually, I think the problem is that `tracked_swap` consumes the tracked references. Let me try a different approach - just directly assign:

